From 8b81f6ce964d0690ba6a9942b17a5e8a852e941c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: samsung: exynos-pmu: undo the C2 programming on
 CPU_PM_ENTER_FAILED

The CPU PM notifier runs first (INT_MAX) and programs the CPU_INFORM C2
hint and the wakeup routing on CPU_PM_ENTER. If a later notifier refuses
the transition, cpu_pm_enter() rolls back with CPU_PM_ENTER_FAILED, which
was ignored: the hint stayed set while the CPU went back to the idle
loop, so the next plain WFI looked like a C2 request to the power
management firmware, which then powers the core off without its context
saved.

Treat CPU_PM_ENTER_FAILED like CPU_PM_EXIT.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
index 9ec2caafd5..13919ae319 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
@@ -324,6 +324,14 @@ static int exynos_cpu_pm_notify_callback(struct notifier_block *self,
 	case CPU_PM_ENTER:
 		return exynos_cpu_pmu_offline();
 
+	/*
+	 * A notifier after us refused CPU_PM_ENTER: the CPU is not going to
+	 * be powered down after all, so undo the C2 hint and the wakeup
+	 * routing. Otherwise the CPU_INFORM C2 hint stays set and the next
+	 * plain WFI of this CPU looks like a C2 request to the firmware, which
+	 * then powers the core off without its context being saved.
+	 */
+	case CPU_PM_ENTER_FAILED:
 	case CPU_PM_EXIT:
 		return exynos_cpu_pmu_online();
 	}
